// CROWN — an install whose handled instance arrives LATER, through a HOF
// parameter: `g(f) = (f()) ~> holder`, the caller's closure stores a
// performing function in holder's state and fires it, under `with !E`.
// Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Checked clean and ran at 7 through the pinned boot (measured 2026-09-23).
// The install unifies the handled instance with the body's performed
// instances ONCE, at g's judgment, when f's row is still empty; the
// instance that reaches the body through f's root at the call site never
// meets holder's. A mask must carry the handled instance and every arrival
// across it must unify with it.
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect Feed { set(k: () -> Int), fire() -> Int }
handler holder with s = () => 0 {
  set(k) => resume() with s = k,
  fire() => resume(s()),
}
fn g(f) = (f()) ~> holder
fn bad() with !E = g(() => {
  set(() => op())
  fire()
})
handler eh { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = (bad()) ~> eh
